#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:5
#: b41822a6f47d4aedbb263a6f64183084
msgid "Safety Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:10
#: 21a3d6062578496eb3ea70ab9bbc531d
msgid "A safety switch can be used to enable/disable the outputs to motors and servos. The switch controls the \"Safety\" state of the vehicle. When in this state, motors are prevented from operating (except in Plane's MANUAL mode if force armed and the :ref:`BRD_SAFETY_MASK <BRD_SAFETY_MASK>` enables outputs controlling the motors), a pre-arm error condition is generated to prevent accidental arming, and servo outputs have their PWM disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:12
#: 1825be726fd54582a61eeb356b3fd544
msgid "the boards' hardware definition file must include this feature. it cannot be added by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:15
#: 8afab41bbb83467b83a8be08cb11f6a0
msgid "LED meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:17
#: bff04b8446b54d4d9978bdb859270eec
msgid "Constant blinking - system is initialising"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:18
#: 807df1a4512d4601ad8ab8393e43cf71
msgid "Intermittent blinking - system is ready but in the \"Safety\" state.  press the safety switch to enable output to the motors and control surfaces if already armed, or to cancel the pre-arm error condition that prevents arming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:19
#: 99de3e09499643ecbdbba2fafbb5322f
msgid "Solid - safety switch has been pressed, motors and servos are able to move once the vehicle is armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:22
#: a2a8d6afb17742abaffb4555e8dca5ff
msgid "Configuring the Safety Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:24
#: 07c46ad01d90484599205e2fb4be013c
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT <BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT>` = 0 to disable the switch for systems not equipped.(``BRD_SAFETYENABLE`` in older firmware versions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:25
#: 240287b47a6b481f9a10942adbc15084
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SAFETYOPTION<BRD_SAFETYOPTION>`. This bitmask controls the behavior of the safety button. It allows you to control if the safety button can be used to enable the safety safety state and/or disable it, and whether the button is only active when disarmed, and to force entry back to the safety on state when you disarm. The default behaviour is for the button to enter or exit the safety state, only when disarmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:26
#: 3f11c468e61e44b786e75c25e9fd7e67
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SAFETY_MASK <BRD_SAFETY_MASK>` can be used to set which individual channels remain enabled with the safety switch. This allows limited control surface movements to check correct operation on the ground. Motor outputs will remain disabled in all stabilized flight modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:28
#: 80c953986cf644909f3a2b66ada3a70d
msgid "Being in the \"Safety\" state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:33
#: 8352639d65524f51a4ce5d6a45d8d090
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SAFETYOPTION<BRD_SAFETYOPTION>` This bitmask controls the operational limits of the safety button. It allows you to control if the safety button can be used for \"Safety\" state enable and/or disable, and whether the button is active if armed. Also, if the \"Safety\" state is forced on upon disarming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:36
#: 101845bd9e09403cbbe5694a1be62b3a
msgid "Using the Safety Switch to force I/O board firmware update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:38
#: 82992d2480e940d180c23d0618c02549
msgid "If the safety switch is held down for the first few seconds after the autopilot is powered up, the I/O firmware is reloaded, if the autopilot includes an IOMCU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:40
#: 35a400ed18ca4a61ac2767d2736dc36b
msgid "This is normally not required but in some rare cases is required after a firmware upload if you hear the \"Start up Failed\" sound after startup (see :ref:`Sounds wiki page <common-sounds-pixhawkpx4>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-safety-switch-pixhawk.rst:44
#: 143477a3881f4794ab26a8cd4136cdaf
msgid "Many autopilots have two CPUs, the main CPU (aka FMU) is where ArduPilot runs. The IOMCU is a separate I/O CPU which is responsible for some I/O including PWM outputs to the MAIN OUT channels. Other autopilots do not have an IOMCU, just the main CPU."
msgstr ""
